  "lesson": {
    "slug": "diag-science-class-1",
    "subject": "science",
    "title": "Science Check-In: Where Am I?",
    "summary": "Explore living things, plants, materials, weather and forces so we can see what you already know about the world.",
    "age_band": "7-8",
    "difficulty": 1,
    "estimated_minutes": 60,
    "unit": "Week 1: Where am I?",
    "learning_objectives": [
      "Show what I know about living things and plants",
      "Show what I know about materials and weather",
      "Show what I know about pushes and pulls"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "diagnostic",
      "week-1"
    ],
    "curriculum": {
      "course": "science-class-1",
      "semester": 1,
      "week": 1
    }
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Welcome, Young Scientist!"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "Scientists ask questions and look closely at the world. Today is a **check-in**, not a test. Have a go at everything and tell a grown-up what you notice."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "emoji": "🔬",
      "alt": "Let's explore!",
      "caption": "Let's explore!"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 1: Living things"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "Living things **grow**, **need food and water**, **move**, **have babies** and **sense** the world. Animals, plants and people are living. Rocks, toys and water are not living."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "prompt": "Which one is living?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "A rock"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "A tree"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "A toy car"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "b"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 2: Animals"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "Animals can be sorted into groups. **Mammals** have fur or hair and feed their babies milk. **Birds** have feathers and wings. **Fish** live in water and have gills. **Insects** have six legs."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "prompt": "Which animal is a bird?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "Penguin"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "Dolphin"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "Ant"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "a"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 3: Plants"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "Plants have **roots** that drink water, a **stem** that holds them up, **leaves** that catch sunlight and often **flowers** that make seeds. Plants need sunlight, water and air to grow."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "prompt": "Which part of a plant drinks water from the soil?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "Leaves"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "Flower"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "Roots"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "c"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "activity",
      "title": "Seed hunt",
      "materials": [
        "a fruit such as an apple or orange",
        "a plate"
      ],
      "instructions": [
        "Ask a grown-up to cut the fruit open.",
        "Find the seeds. How many can you count?",
        "Think: what might each seed grow into?"
      ]
    },
