    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 4: Materials"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "Things are made from **materials**. Glass is see-through and breakable. Metal is hard and shiny. Wood is strong. Rubber stretches. We pick materials that suit the job: a raincoat is **waterproof**."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "prompt": "Which material is best for a window?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "Wood"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "Glass"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "text": "Wool"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "b"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Stop 5: Weather and forces"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "markdown": "Weather can be sunny, rainy, windy, cloudy or snowy. A **force** is a push or a pull. We push a door open and pull a wagon."
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "question": {
        "type": "multiple_choice",
        "prompt": "Kicking a ball is a...",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "text": "Push"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "text": "Pull"
          }
        ],
        "answer": [
          "a"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "reveal",
      "prompt": "What do you think happens to a puddle on a sunny day?",
      "answer_markdown": "The Sun warms the water and it slowly turns into an invisible gas in the air. This is called evaporation."
    },
    {
      "type": "brain_game",
      "game": "memory_match",
      "title": "Find the living things",
      "goal": "Match the pairs of animals and plants.",
      "emojis": [
        "🐶",
        "🐟",
        "🐦",
        "🐛",
        "🌻",
        "🌳"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "summary",
      "points": [
        "Living things grow, need food and water, and have babies.",
        "Plants have roots, stems, leaves and flowers.",
        "Different materials suit different jobs.",
        "A force is a push or a pull."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "style": "tip",
      "markdown": "Ready? Start the quiz. There are 12 questions and about 15 minutes. If you are not sure, take your best guess!"
    },
    {
      "type": "glossary",
      "terms": [
        {
          "term": "check-in",
          "meaning": "A friendly game that shows us what you know. It is not a test."
        },
        {
          "term": "mammal",
          "meaning": "An animal with fur or hair that feeds its babies milk, like a dog or a cow."
        },
        {
          "term": "insect",
          "meaning": "A small animal with 6 legs, like an ant or a bee."
        },
        {
          "term": "roots",
          "meaning": "The part of a plant under the ground that drinks water."
        },
        {
          "term": "stem",
          "meaning": "The part of a plant that holds it up and carries water."
        },
        {
          "term": "force",
          "meaning": "A push or a pull."
        },
        {
          "term": "waterproof",
          "meaning": "Water cannot get through it."
        },
        {
          "term": "materials",
          "meaning": "What things are made of, like wood, metal or plastic."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
